    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "105 Harmonstown Road presents an excellent opportunity to acquire a well-located three-bedroom mid-terrace home in one of Dublin 5's most established and convenient residential areas. Harmonstown Road is a mature neighbourhood popular with families and commuters alike, within walking distance of Harmonstown DART Station, local schools, shops, parks and a wide range of everyday amenities.\r\n\r\nThe accommodation extends to a bright and practical layout comprising an entrance hallway, spacious living room, kitchen/dining area, three bedrooms and a family bathroom.\r\n\r\nOutside, the property benefits from a private rear garden offering excellent potential for outdoor entertaining.\r\n\r\nA standout feature is the off-street parking to the front, with a private driveway providing valuable parking space and added convenience.\r\n\r\nThe location is second to none, with excellent transport links including nearby DART and bus services, while Artane Castle Shopping Centre, schools, sporting facilities, cafés and numerous local amenities are all within easy reach. Harmonstown and Artane continue to be highly sought-after locations due to their accessibility, family-friendly atmosphere and proximity to Dublin City Centre."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Accommodation :\r\n\r\nFoyer : 1.71m x 3.60m\r\n\r\nLiving Room : 3.62m x 3.60m\r\n\r\nFamily Room : 3.16m x 3.02m\r\n\r\nDining Area : 2.17m x 3.02m\r\n\r\nKitchen : 2.44m x 2.25m \r\n\r\nMain bedroom : 3.42m x 3.83m \r\n\r\nBedroom 2 : 4.11m x 2.79m\r\n\r\nBedroom 3 : 2.86m x 2.79m\r\n\r\nBathroom : 2.17m x 2.12m"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "350 metres to Harmonstown DART Station\r\n\r\nOff-street parking on private front driveway\r\n\r\nWell-established residential location\r\n\r\nPrivate rear garden\r\n\r\nClose to schools, shops, parks and sporting facilities\r\n\r\nEasy access to Dublin City Centre, M1, M50 and Dublin Airport"
      },
